WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.200
Whether they broke things off quickly or they're
still happily married with five kids, these

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.941
fictional relatives ended up in very real
relationships.

00:00:09.329 --> 00:00:14.049
Anna Kendrick and Bill Hader play the adult
children of Santa Claus who save Christmas

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:17.590
in the 2019 Disney+ holiday movie "Noelle."

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:22.130
This stint as festive movie siblings led to
a romantic relationship off the screen.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.449
A source told Us Weekly —

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:25.230
"Bill and Anna clicked right away.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.980
They dig each other's sense of humor."

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.970
The source made sure to clarify that nothing
happened between the two until they were both

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.669
single at the same time.

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:37.721
Hader got a divorce from his wife Maggie Carey
in 2018 — and before dating Kendrick, he

00:00:37.721 --> 00:00:41.829
had a relationship with Rachel Bilson, his
co-star in "The To Do List."

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:47.120
In January 2022, sources revealed that Kendrick
and Hader were dating and had been keeping

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.649
their relationship under wraps for under a
year.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:54.140
According to Cosmopolitan's math, Kendrick
and Hader got together sometime between July

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.989
2020 and December 2020.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:01:00.220
With speculation about the status of their
relationship rife, a source told ET —

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.330
"Bill and Anna are in love and very happy
in their relationship, and enjoying their

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.420
time together."

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.181
Hader didn't respond to the comments, choosing
to keep their relationship private for the

00:01:09.181 --> 00:01:11.270
sake of his daughters.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.420
Unfortunately, things just didn't last for
these on-screen sibs, with ET reporting that

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.140
the two broke up in June 2022.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.984
It's unlikely that we'll see Kendrick appear
in any of Hader's future projects.

00:01:21.984 --> 00:01:25.135
"Lots of guest stars here tonight — could
we ever see Anna Kendrick as a guest star?"

00:01:25.135 --> 00:01:25.800
"Oh…

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.300
no."

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:26.921
"No way?" [nervous laughter]

00:01:26.921 --> 00:01:27.921
"No way?"

00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:33.170
After seven years on "Gilmore Girls," Lauren
Graham took a small break from TV before taking

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:37.060
on the role of another single mom in the comedy-drama
"Parenthood."

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:43.150
Graham's Sarah Braverman is the mom to Mae
Whitman's Amber and Miles Heizer's Drew.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:48.090
She also shares the screen with "9-1-1" star
Peter Krause, who plays her brother, Adam.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.526
The two play siblings in the series, but it
didn't stop them from falling in love in real life.

00:01:52.526 --> 00:01:57.904
Graham has her "Gilmore Girls" TV mom, Kelly
Bishop, to thank for encouraging her to date Krause.

00:01:57.904 --> 00:02:02.400
The pair obviously had a natural chemistry,
but Graham has said that they were both hesitant

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.009
to act on it because of past unsuccessful
relationships they'd had with co-stars.

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:10.679
After having worked together for a while on
"Parenthood” though, they decided to take

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:11.860
the plunge.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.400
Ultimately, Graham felt that working in the
same industry actually ended up being of benefit.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.400
The actor told People —

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.010
"It's hard to explain to people when you have
a fancy job like being an actor what is challenging

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.010
about it.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:26.340
So we just kind of have that shorthand, a
shared language, which is helpful."

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.250
Their differences eventually caught up with
them, and they ended up separating after more

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.730
than a decade together.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:35.670
During their relationship, Graham took on
an important step-motherly role in the life

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:41.219
of Krause's son Roman — something she plans
to continue even after their 2021 break-up.

00:02:41.415 --> 00:02:45.819
David Tennant has played some impressive roles
throughout his career, including Barty Crouch

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:51.110
Jr. in "Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire,"
Kilgrave in "Jessica Jones," and Crowley in

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.110
"Good Omens."

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:57.809
Of course, his most iconic role will always
be that of the tenth Doctor in the BBC's "Doctor Who."

00:02:57.809 --> 00:03:01.750
It was the role that kept on giving — it
introduced him to Georgia Moffett, the woman

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.225
who would eventually become Mrs. Georgia Tennant.

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:05.648
There's just one thing, though…

00:03:05.648 --> 00:03:11.263
"She's… well… she's my daughter."

00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:14.514
"Hello, Dad."

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.180
The fictional relation didn't seem to bother
them: the pair started dating in 2008, and

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.340
they married at the end of 2011.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.340
David Tennant admitted to The Independent
—

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.879
"Because Doctor Who had run through my life
like a stick of rock, to end up marrying the

00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:32.040
daughter of one of the doctors, it all felt
a bit stupid — there were a lot of things

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.040
against it."

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.340
Moffett, who is the real-life daughter of
fifth Doctor actor Peter Davison, didn't give

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.319
up on their connection — and it all worked
out in the end.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.319
Tennant continued —

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:45.310
"You reach a point of your life when you're
looking for someone and it's sort of chance

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.220
which version of that perfect partner ambles
along."

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:53.819
As of 2023, the actors are still happily married
and share five kids together, including "House

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:55.510
of the Dragon's" Ty Tennant.

00:03:56.523 --> 00:04:03.300
Milo Ventimiglia starred in "Heroes" from
2006 to 2010 as Peter Petrelli, who turns

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.850
out to be the uncle of Hayden Panettiere's
Claire Bennet.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:11.110
Their familial status in the series didn't
stop their off-screen connection, though;

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:18.799
the pair dated from 2007 to 2009 — just
a year after Ventimiglia had separated from Alexis Bledel.

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:23.785
Panettiere had also recently ended her two-year
relationship with "Laguna Beach" star Stephen Colletti.

00:04:23.785 --> 00:04:27.560
A family friend confirmed their relationship
in 2007, telling People —

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.820
"Hayden's mom adores Milo.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.180
She thinks he's so cute.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.510
She tells her friends that he's her boyfriend.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.510
She's very proud."

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:38.229
To some fans, however, the age gap in their
relationship was controversial.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:42.530
Panettiere was just 18 when they began dating,
while Ventimiglia was 29.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:47.680
At the time, Ventimiglia didn't want to fan
the media flames of their relationship, denying

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.830
anything romantic and claiming they were just
good friends.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.280
Ventimiglia and Panettiere ended up staying
together for almost two years.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.000
Although they did not publicly comment on
their split, another source told People —

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.440
"They lead different lifestyles.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.699
He's 31, she's 19.

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:05.520
She still has growing up to do and he's very
low-key."

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.990
According to the outlet, the pair remained
cordial, and they continued to work on "Heroes"

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.717
together until the show ended.

00:05:11.717 --> 00:05:16.780
Barry Williams and Maureen McCormick are more
often recognized as Greg and Marcia — two

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:21.980
of the siblings from "The Brady Bunch," which
aired from 1969 to 1974.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.300
Tales of their off-screen relationship are
infamous, and the pair have both been open

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.340
about their time together over the years.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:32.750
In fact, McCormick and Williams enjoyed their
first kiss together while shooting the first

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:37.169
episode of Season 4 in Hawaii, as the actors
revealed during an appearance on "Watch What

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:38.169
Happens Live!"

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:40.140
"Scale of one to ten."

00:05:43.238 --> 00:05:44.274
"Ten.

00:05:44.274 --> 00:05:46.409
Wow!"

00:05:46.409 --> 00:05:50.919
McCormick revealed in her book, "Here's the
Story: Surviving Marcia Brady and Finding

00:05:50.919 --> 00:05:51.919
My True Voice" —

00:05:51.919 --> 00:05:56.449
"There was so much electricity between us
that I felt the hair on my arms stand up every

00:05:56.449 --> 00:05:57.830
time we got close to each other...

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.100
I thought about Barry even when I had other
scenes with other guys.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:05.750
I used to ask myself how I could ever look
in eyes other than his liquid blues and feel

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:06.688
such love."

00:06:06.688 --> 00:06:10.870
However, their intense attraction did make
it difficult when filming a scene later in

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.560
Season 4 in which the teen actors had to sit
on the bed together.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.769
McCormick admitted —

00:06:15.769 --> 00:06:17.752
"We couldn't keep our hands off each other."

00:06:17.752 --> 00:06:22.259
Despite their strong feelings, the on-off
relationship between these on-screen siblings

00:06:22.259 --> 00:06:23.259
didn't work.

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:26.750
It eventually fizzled out, with McCormick
saying that timing got in their way.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:31.210
There are no hard feelings, though: the former
couple are still close friends decades after

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.210
their split.

00:06:32.498 --> 00:06:37.729
Emily VanCamp and Chris Pratt are both known
for starring in the MCU, with VanCamp playing

00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:42.449
SHIELD agent Sharon Carter and Pratt traversing
the galaxy as Star-Lord.

00:06:42.449 --> 00:06:47.800
But over a decade before their superhero adventures,
the actors worked together on the show "Everwood"

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:52.120
playing siblings Amy and Bright Abbott — and
they fell in love on set.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:57.419
In 2006, Pratt admitted that he felt a little
weirded out starting a romantic relationship

00:06:57.419 --> 00:06:59.949
with his on-screen sister — as did fans.

00:06:59.949 --> 00:07:01.240
He told TV Guide —

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:05.860
"Yeah, we've pretty much gotten used to the
response of, 'Eww, that's weird.'

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:09.610
The people who know us are happy, and probably
expected it to happen eventually.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:13.890
But yeah, every once in a while we get that
one person that's like, 'That's really creepy.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.770
You just kissed your sister.'"

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.990
VanCamp and Pratt ultimately ignored the haters
and let their love blossom, dating from 2004

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:23.940
to 2007 before going their separate ways.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:29.650
As of 2023, VanCamp is happily married to
her "Revenge" co-star Josh Bowman, with whom

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:30.951
she shares a daughter.

00:07:30.951 --> 00:07:35.889
Meanwhile, Pratt also has three kids: a son
with his ex, Anna Faris, and two daughters

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:38.160
with his wife, Katherine Schwarzenegger.

00:07:38.643 --> 00:07:43.710
Before she married Josh Bowman but after dating
Chris Pratt, Emily VanCamp dated another of

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:47.949
her on-screen siblings: her "Brothers and
Sisters" co-star, Dave Annable.

00:07:47.949 --> 00:07:52.590
Before Annable met his now-wife Odette during
the show's fifth season, the pair dated for

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:53.590
over a year.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.400
When the show kicks off, VanCamp's character
Rebecca is shown to be the half-sister of

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:04.249
Annable's character Justin, but this storyline
was later changed by the series creator, Greg Berlanti.

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:06.471
Berlanti told Entertainment Weekly —

00:08:06.471 --> 00:08:09.949
"I looked like an idiot ... Here were two
young people who didn't grow up with each

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:12.650
other, didn't know each other, but they had
this electricity.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.139
There was nothing I could do."

00:08:14.139 --> 00:08:18.430
In the second season of "Brothers &amp; Sisters,"
Rebecca discovers she's not a member of the

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:22.020
Walker clan after all, which leaves her and
Justin free to date.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:27.146
The shocking twist was a welcome storyline
for the real-life couple: VanCamp told EW —

00:08:27.146 --> 00:08:30.639
"I'm all for breaking boundaries, but we didn't
need to get into incest.

00:08:30.639 --> 00:08:32.610
I draw the line at that."

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:38.479
Regardless, it didn't last: VanCamp and Annable
called it quits in 2008 but continued working

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:41.836
together until she departed the series in
2010.

00:08:41.836 --> 00:08:47.270
In 2006, Jennifer Carpenter and Michael C.
Hall met on the set of "Dexter."

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.540
Hall played the titular Dexter Morgan, while
Carpenter played his sister, Debra.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:56.220
At some point between their first meeting
and 2008, the pair got together — and their

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.700
romance only intensified, culminating with
a marriage on New Year's Eve that year.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.770
Around that time, Carpenter told On Demand
Entertainment —

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.960
"We had a great base for our relationship.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:10.510
We see each other on a day-to-day basis and
you know, I know him and he knows me."

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:14.682
The fact that they played siblings didn't
seem to get in the way or make things weird, either.

00:09:14.682 --> 00:09:20.720
Things got serious in 2009 when Hall was diagnosed
with Hodgkin's Lymphoma, and Carpenter supported

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.420
him until he reached remission.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:26.340
The pair seemed stronger than ever — but
sadly, it simply wasn't meant to be.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:32.300
They divorced in 2011, but continued to play
siblings on the show until it ended in 2013

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:35.950
— and they reunited for the limited series
sequel, "Dexter: New Blood."

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:39.560
Carpenter told Today that they will always
have a close friendship, saying —

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:43.696
"Just because the marriage ended doesn't mean
the love isn't still there."

00:09:43.696 --> 00:09:45.910
Katherine Heigl goes by many names.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:50.410
To a lot of her fans, she's the queen of romantic
comedies from the 2000s, while others will

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.250
always see her as Izzie Stevens from "Grey's
Anatomy."

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:58.860
Before all of that, though, she was Isabel
Evans in the sci-fi drama "Roswell" from 1999

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:04.010
to 2002, alongside Shiri Appleby, Brendan
Fehr, and Jason Behr.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:06.730
Behr played her on-screen adopted brother,
Max.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:11.510
Isabel and Max were close — but not as close
as Heigl and Behr, who dated off-screen for

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.940
most of the show's run.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.769
Although they largely kept their relationship
out of the public eye during that time, there

00:10:16.769 --> 00:10:22.170
was enough attention on the actors to spark
romance rumors before they split in 2002.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:26.290
Behr soon moved on from their relationship
after meeting fellow actor KaDee Strickland

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.970
on the set of "The Grudge" in 2004.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:33.030
They tied the knot in 2006 and welcomed a
son in 2020.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:38.490
Heigl also got engaged in 2006, marrying musician
Josh Kelley the following year.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.490
They have three children.

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:44.901
Before she became a household name for starring
opposite Patrick Swayze in "Dirty Dancing,"

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:49.160
Jennifer Grey played Jeannie Bueller in the
beloved '80s teen comedy "Ferris Bueller's

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.540
Day Off" alongside Matthew Broderick.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:56.189
As Ferris and Jeannie, Broderick and Grey
portray a tumultuous sibling relationship

00:10:56.189 --> 00:10:59.470
— but their relationship off-screen was
much less strained.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.760
Grey admitted in her memoir, "Out of the Corner"
—

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:06.680
"I was as surprised as anyone when our relationship
morphed from on-screen sibling rivalry to

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.590
off-screen illicit romance."

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:12.750
The couple did everything they could to keep
their romance under wraps, stealing away moments

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:13.940
together on set.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.687
They were so enamored with each other that
they became engaged before filming had even ended.

00:11:18.687 --> 00:11:21.358
"Heh… oh, kids!"

00:11:21.358 --> 00:11:25.850
Grey later revealed that her career-defining
role in "Dirty Dancing" took its toll on their

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.140
relationship, admitting that she felt unsupported
by Broderick.

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:32.450
At this point, the couple was still hiding
their relationship — but the truth came

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:37.709
tumbling out when they were involved in a
serious car crash in Northern Ireland in 1987.

00:11:37.709 --> 00:11:41.300
This signaled the beginning of the end for
the couple, who called it quits the following

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.860
year without tying the knot.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:47.019
Broderick eventually went on to marry "Sex
and the City" star Sarah Jessica Parker, while

00:11:47.019 --> 00:11:50.010
Grey rebounded by getting engaged to Johnny
Depp.

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:54.370
They didn't end up together in the end, though,
as Grey shared 19 years of marriage with Marvel

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:58.140
star Clark Gregg before announcing their separation
in 2020.

